            "review_title": "Review at La Vong Grilled Fish",
            "review_text": "Sonya M\n16 contributions\n0\nGreat local dish\nDec 2024 • Family\nThis is a traditional cha ca restaurant. There are no menus. They serve one dish and one dish only. Beverages are beer, water and whatever soda they have on hand. The fish is cooked at the table in a skillet with fresh herbs and vermicelli. We didn’t know what we were doing and the owner of the restaurant took pity on us and showed us (we were a table of 8). It was delicious. Not for everyone but if you’re adventurous and willing to eat as the llocals eat, then head to this place. I found this place through a recommendation from Hana at the Tirant Hotel - this is where she takes her family. We ended up eating here twice despite agreeing not to do repeats. It was that good. This is the original creator of this dish. The restaurant is 153 years old and serves the same recipe since its creation. The street is named after this restaurant. If you are looking for a meal that the locals, definitely give this place a try.\nRead more\nInsider tip:\nVery limited drink menu. Saigon beer is served warm in the can. I would bring my own beverage.\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nWritten December 27, 2024",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-15",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
        },
