            "review_text": "Michelle N\n20 contributions\n0\nA favorite for many decades\nJun 2023 • Family\nI've been coming to this place with my parents since I was a little child, and I'm now in my 30s. It's our family tradition. We love this place, and it's been written about in the NYT\n\nIt's a very old house (typical for the Old Quarter), but the dining room is air conditioned. The stairs are tiny because Vietnamese people are small, but just go slowly!\n\nThere is only one dish. You eat by mixing the herbs in with the fish, and then in a small bowl you gather vermicelli, a few peanuts, a dollop of shrimp paste, a few pieces of fish and maybe one teaspoon of oil from the pan. Mix them all up, and you have yourself a delicious dish! The quality has stayed consistent for the last ~20+ years. \n\nYes, it is 'more expensive' than the other street food in Hanoi, but still it's maybe $8/serving, and you'd probably need 2. Seems cheap to me!\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nWritten June 23, 2023",
